@* Decision 0011 (W3 fix): the <head> content both layouts share (_Layout and the setup wizard's _SetupLayout), kept in one place: the
   charset and viewport, the title, Web.Common's _WebCommonHead (the favicon, theme-boot.js before the first paint, Bootstrap and the PiSharp
   tokens), then Settings › Appearance (run W3, unit AP: appearance.js, a classic script after theme-boot.js, sets this browser's theme,
   font size, density, code theme and chat display options on <html> before the first paint; appearance.css reads them) and site.css. A
   layout renders its page's Styles section after it. No inline script (the Content-Security-Policy has script-src 'self'). Model: the
   page's title (string). *@
@model string
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>@Model · PiSharp Web Agent</title>
<partial name="_WebCommonHead" model='"pisharp-theme"' />
<script src="~/js/appearance.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<link href="~/css/appearance.css" rel="stylesheet" asp-append-version="true">
<link href="~/css/site.css" rel="stylesheet" asp-append-version="true">
